ACCEPTANCE 4 - theme toggle after render keeps the filtered chart
STATUS: PARTLY MET -- the stated direction holds, the reverse direction
        REGRESSES.  *** THIS IS THE FAIL ***
------------------------------------------------------------
  The stated claim holds. insightChartMarkers() (insights.js:353-359) returns
  [{color: accent}, {color: prior, pattern:{shape:'/'}}] - SCALARS, no
  per-point array - and the themechange handler calls
  Plotly.restyle(chart, {marker: markers}), touching only `marker`, never
  x/y. Empirically, flipping the theme while expanded kept the categories
  identical (cats-equal: True, n=41 and n=33) in every case. The restyle
  cannot resurrect hidden bars: CONFIRMED.

  FAILING BEHAVIOUR (new in this attempt, not on master):
  Because trendsChartRaw is frozen at htmx:afterRequest time with the markers
  of the theme that was active AT FETCH TIME, and renderTrendsChart() now
  re-renders from trendsChartRaw on EVERY table interaction, any expand /
  collapse / sort performed after a theme toggle repaints the chart in the
  STALE theme's colours.

  Reproduction, worker build (blob 41c3da6), page loaded light then
  #theme-toggle clicked to dark:
    after theme->dark   : dark=true bars=12 m0="rgb(165,180,252)" m1="#a8a29e"
    after expand (dark) : dark=true bars=41 m0="rgb(79,70,229)"  m1="#78716c"
    after sort   (dark) : dark=true bars=41 m0="rgb(79,70,229)"  m1="#78716c"

  Same probe against the MASTER baseline build (blob 563bf12, same server,
  same port, rebuilt):
    after theme->dark   : dark=true bars=41 m0="rgb(165,180,252)" m1="#a8a29e"
    after expand (dark) : dark=true bars=41 m0="rgb(165,180,252)" m1="#a8a29e"
    after sort   (dark) : dark=true bars=41 m0="rgb(165,180,252)" m1="#a8a29e"
  -> master keeps the dark colours through expand and sort. The regression is
     introduced by TC1, it is not pre-existing.

  Reproduced in 10 of the 52 matrix states, all of them dark-page states
  reached through a table interaction:
    janaug.dark.{expanded,collapsed,sort_current,sort_category,
                 sort_category_expanded}
    june.dark.{expanded,collapsed,sort_current,sort_category,
               sort_category_expanded}
  In every one: document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark') === true
  while marker0 == rgb(79,70,229) (light indigo-600) and marker1 ==
  #78716c (light stone-500).

  Impact, computed on the dark card background #292524 (stone-800):
    light accent   #4f46e5 on #292524 -> 2.41:1   (below the 3:1 non-text
                                                   minimum, WCAG 2.2 1.4.11)
    correct accent #a5b4fc on #292524 -> 7.61:1
    light prior    #78716c on #292524 -> 3.16:1
    correct prior  #a8a29e on #292524 -> 6.01:1
  BL4 chose stone-400/stone-500 per theme deliberately; this path discards
  that choice. It also contradicts TC1 contract item 1, "markers applied as
  today": on master the rendered markers always match the CURRENT theme.

  WHAT IS MISSING (for the worker, not fixed here): renderTrendsChart() must
  apply the CURRENT insightChartMarkers() to the filtered copy before calling
  renderChart, instead of inheriting the markers frozen into trendsChartRaw
  at fetch time. A regression test should assert marker colour after
  toggle-then-expand in dark.

